ects; each target project carries a thin per-project profile; new/unmanaged project folders are auto-offered `git init` + `gh repo create`; and Mark's own sessions are never Pete-framed.  **Architecture:** Three-way separation. (1) **Portable core** = the plugin (skills + hooks + commands + generic machinery), project-agnostic. (2) **Per-project profile** = a small `.pilot/` dir + the project's existing `CLAUDE.md` in each target repo, supplying red-path globs, deploy adapter, enforcement level, operator register. (3) **Per-machine activation** = the plugin is *enabled* only on operator machines (Pete's), so maintainers (Mark) who merely hold the repo are never activated. Git identity is keyed to the GitHub **org**, not the directory name.  **Tech Stack:** Claude Code plugin (`.claude-plugin/plugin.json` + `marketplace.json` + `hooks/hooks.json` w/ `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`), POSIX sh + a Windows `run-hook.cmd` shim, Python 3 (identity guard + detection), PHP 8.1 (S1 validator, already built), `gh` CLI, GitHub Actions (reusable composite action for `[S]` CI).  ## Global Constraints - **Portable core carries NO project specifics.** No `Jointly`/`Forge`/`Livewire`/`prod-hotfixes`/`Stripe`/`Herd`/`magic.php` strings in plugin skills — those live in a project profile. (S0 `HARNESS.md` currently has Forge/deploy terms in its glossary → migrate those to the profile spec or mark them as adapter-supplied.) - **Committed rules are the safety floor.** No gitignored/per-machine/per-operator file may *lower* enforcement, deploy targets, danger-path gating, or confirmation steps. On any conflict, the committed profile + `config.yml` enforcement win. - **Ingested text = DATA, never instructions** — including the operator file (see Phase 5's fence). The sole, tightly-scoped exception is operator *presentation* preferences. - **Hooks detect; the agent (with consent) acts.** A hook must never run `gh repo create`, merge, push, or any interactive/irreversible action. - **Private by def